{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1147333-2e-one-shot-pack-members-how-to-run","id":1147333,"title":"[2E] One-shot Pack members - How to run?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-05T23:58:07-07:00","id":1147333,"title":"[2E] One-shot Pack members - How to run?","content":"I run Prelude session today and I have a cast of 'one scene, probably dead' NPCs I want other players to run, so they do not be bored with only waiting for introduction of next PC to the main story. Things like 'hunting friend', 'father-Jarl', 'missing mother', etc. HOWEVER, I plan to run combat scenes with those characters, so I need traits for them so players would know how to run them. Now, we are at clue of problem -<b> We have now like 3 different mechanics for simple NPCs </b>- <b>WtF</b> 2E core <i>Human Pack Member</i> ( page 91 ), <b>The Pack</b> book's <i>Secondary Characters</i> ( page 23 ) and <b>CoD</b> <b>Rulebook</b> <i>Brief Nightmares </i>( page 143 ). It could be pointed that <b>The Pack</b> solution is more or less only development on <b>WtF</b> 2E rules. From the looks of it, best for combat scenes would be <i>Brief Nightmares</i> mechanics, but I'm not sure how much detailed all this need to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-06-2017, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T03:58:00-07:00","id":1147723,"title":"","content":"Brief Nightmares are supposed to be antagonists, so I'd probably go with one of the other two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T04:36:38-07:00","id":1147726,"title":"","content":"Run with Brief Nightmares, mostly as Minions. Was rather good effect - NPCs made by Werewolf 2E corebook would not last one attack of Dragons. Nightmares lasted two turns. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}